name: consensus
description: Dual-agent consensus workflow for moderate-or-higher-complexity work — planning, implementation, debugging, investigation, migrations, refactors, operational change — where one agent authors and the other independently reviews, per step, to consensus. Bind IMPLEMENTER=CLAUDE when the request says Claude should build it; IMPLEMENTER=CODEX when it says Codex should build it; otherwise use the project's declared default and ask if the choice materially changes the result. Use when the user asks for the consensus workflow, dual review, or "you build it and have the other one check it". Exempt only an unchanged already-approved diff, an obvious one-line correction, a mechanical rename, formatting-only work, or equivalently bounded judgment-free work; classify everything else as moderate+.
